Original commit body from e76af78:

When --frameworks all was specified, the profile detection still scanned
dependency files to detect frameworks. This meant that if a framework wasn't
listed in requirements.txt/package.json but its decorators were present in
code, no entrypoint patterns would match.

Now --frameworks all uses ALL known framework patterns for detected languages,
enabling entrypoint detection even when frameworks aren't in manifest files.

Bug discovered by 12.10 bakeoff experiment after removing legacy _detect_*
functions - with legacy removal, --frameworks none and --frameworks all both
produced 0 entrypoints because the "all" mode wasn't actually loading all
framework patterns.
